# THE ONE THAT ACTUALLY APPLIES.
#
# DEPLOY.md recommends setting Vercel's Root Directory to `game`. Vercel reads
# .vercelignore from the root of the PROJECT, not of the repository — so with that
# setting the .vercelignore at the repo root is never read at all, and every byte of
# source art under game/assets ships to the CDN. Measured: 55MB of GIFs, un-sliced
# sheets and option-shape PNGs that no URL in the game ever requests.
#
# The root .vercelignore stays for the other case (Root Directory left unset, where
# the repo root IS the project). The two files cover the two settings; neither is
# redundant, and losing either one silently uploads the source art.
#
# Everything listed here is the INPUT to a build and never fetched by the game:
#   assets/GIF/*.gif          -> tools/gif-to-grid.mjs         -> assets/char/*-gif.png
#   assets/char/*-gif.png     -> tools/slice-char.mjs          -> assets/char/mammoth-*.webp
#   assets/option-shape/*.png -> tools/build-option-shapes.mjs -> the .webp + the rings
#   assets/art/cover.png      -> tools/assets.mjs              -> assets/art/cover.webp
assets/GIF
assets/char/*-gif.png
assets/option-shape/*.png
assets/art/cover.png

# Parked experiments and the in-repo QA harness pages. Neither is part of the game.
drafts
qa
